Layered architecture:
Drivers - hardware abstraction layer (HAL)
services - mid level logic (PID timming waveform)
application - orchestration layer

All of these are peers in the architecture, they all depend on the lower layers


Architectural rules:

Drivers never know about services - keep dependencies upward only
Services may depend on drivers - TimmingService uses Timer
application depends on services - high level orchestration only 
no stl or heap - everything static or stack-allocated
Deterministic initialize() and update() - every component follows the same pattern


Conceptual Ownership:

core/ - Base interfaces and light weight utilities - no dependencies
drivers/ - Hardware interfacing - depends on core
services/ - combine multiple drivers, logic - depends on drivers and core
app/ - System orchestration, flight modes - depends on services drivers and core
